**Primary use case:**

An organisation connects AI assistants to MCP servers that expose business tools, documents, APIs, and databases. SENTINEL-MCP evaluates requests, enforces authorisation policies, protects sensitive information, records security decisions, and allows security teams to validate their controls through controlled attack simulations.

**Core differentiator:**

This is not only an MCP security dashboard. It combines runtime security enforcement with a dedicated, repeatable testing environment that verifies actual security outcomes.

